1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:03,080
You're leaving already, Lord Odin?

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,106
He may cause trouble,
but I'll still miss him.

3
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:09,717
I heard word there's a
monster living in Kuri.

4
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:11,680
An ogre called Ashura Doji.

5
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:13,710
Hmm.

6
00:00:13,793 --> 00:00:14,886
Kuri's a blight on this land.

7
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:17,180
Even the Shogun cannot control it.

8
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:20,320
If the criminal takes refuge in Kuri,

9
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:22,897
the authorities are
powerless to apprehend him.

10
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:27,457
But if they lack the strength to survive
there, they'll be chewed up and spit out.

11
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:30,920
It's a lawless land, almost
like a different country.

12
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:36,077
Interesting, perhaps I should
take a tour around Wano.

13
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:37,880
Have a safe trip, Odin!

14
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:42,440
Keen, Denjiro, come visit us again.

15
00:00:42,720 --> 00:00:43,720
See ya.

16
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:49,300
He shows up uninvited and leaves just
as suddenly He values his freedom.

17
00:00:49,540 --> 00:00:50,460
Lord Yasui

18
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,140
Come look, hurry

19
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:56,877
This is the room that Lord Odin stayed in.

20
00:00:56,960 --> 00:00:58,977
Why on earth would he do such a thing?

21
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:01,648
We must send him a bill
for repairs at once.

22
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:06,080
Let's just pretend there
was a natural disaster.

23
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:09,735
If you're too soft on him,
he'll take advantage of you.

24
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:10,840
Lord Yasui!

25
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:12,800
What is it now?

26
00:01:14,780 --> 00:01:16,460
The money is missing?

27
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,240
Yes, I'm certain I put it in
the safe, my lord. Um. Hmm?

28
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:24,797
It pains me dearly to say this.

29
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:28,280
But I'm afraid that the money was stolen.

30
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:30,677
I saw it.

31
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,157
It was Lord Odin.

32
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:35,677
He slipped it into his robe
and walked away without a word.

33
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:38,197
I knew it was that scoundrel.

34
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:40,597
Biting the hand that feeds
him is what he's doing.

35
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:41,557
He'll pay.

36
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:43,900
Would Odin bother being sneaky?

37
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:47,400
Are you sure, Orochi?

38
00:01:48,220 --> 00:01:49,740
Yes, forgive me

39
00:01:50,240 --> 00:01:51,360
I was too afraid.

40
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:54,152
I should have made an effort to stop him.

41
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:07,980
After leaving Hakumai, Oden and his
followers continued onward to Kuri,

42
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:10,720
causing trouble all along the way.

43
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:20,957
How much longer are
you going to follow me?

44
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:21,960
Why forever?

45
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:24,729
Because we're your
biggest fans, Lord Odin.

46
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,020
He's annoyed.

47
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:36,457
Hey, why are you standing
in the rain, you idiots?

48
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:40,834
As your retainers, we must protect
you Come on, you're going to get sick.

49
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:41,920
On our way!

50
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:45,348
What are you doing in here?

51
00:02:45,620 --> 00:02:47,020
I am writing a journal.

52
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:49,460
They say it is a navigator's duty.

53
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:51,840
A daily observance on ships overseas.

54
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:57,172
The following are excerpts from Odin's
journal, chronicling his adventures.

55
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:11,780
In Ringo, we met some ragged little
ruts, a pair of starving siblings.

56
00:03:14,580 --> 00:03:15,920
Get out of here!

57
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:24,294
They tried to earn money by dancing,
but people were as cold as the snow.

58
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:33,120
Why do you little agents
keep following me?

59
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:36,240
That food isn't yours.

60
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:38,060
Are you listening?

61
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:39,420
Put that back.

62
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:42,881
They were the children of
a great master of dance.

63
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:46,197
But their families split apart
when their father was arrested.

64
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:50,740
They brazenly ate our Odin without
my permission, sobbing all the while.

65
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:52,580
Impossible to deter.

66
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:06,480
In Koby, there was a goblin of a man who
cut the hair off the living and dead alike,

67
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:08,577
carrying it away into the night.

68
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:13,020
As it turns out, he sold brushes
made from human hair for a living.

69
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,160
Whoa! I give up! I give up!

70
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:25,297
I thought you were dead!

71
00:04:25,380 --> 00:04:29,620
After I gave him a good wallop,
he strangely decided to follow me.

72
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:34,377
He claimed to be a long-suffering victim
of persecution, but he likely deserved it.

73
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:36,280
In the deep forests of Uda,

74
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:40,057
tales of a notorious mountain
bandit were carried on the wind.

75
00:04:40,140 --> 00:04:43,552
They say he would abduct women
and beat men half to death.

76
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:46,700
Why are you following me, too?

77
00:04:47,020 --> 00:04:47,900
Funny, right?

78
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:57,550
Hmm.

79
00:04:57,633 --> 00:04:58,967
Is that the mountain bandit?

80
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:03,760
You're okay!

81
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:08,360
In truth, the bandit was
a skilled ninja, Raizo,

82
00:05:08,660 --> 00:05:13,160
who quit the Kozuki clan's Oniwabanshu
after Okunoichi broke his heart.

83
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:15,960
I can't live my life in hiding anymore!

84
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:17,612
Please take me with you!

85
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:24,240
He's annoyed!

86
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:37,660
Kozuki Oden came here?

87
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:39,700
He's the son of the shogun.

88
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:41,740
Killing him should be fun.

89
00:05:42,060 --> 00:05:44,020
Go and bring him to me. Yes, sir!

90
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:57,440
More than anything, I love to see
the high and mighty brought low.

91
00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:02,140
Hey, where did Odin go?

92
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,840
He went to take a dump,
I think. Been a while.

93
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:07,158
That was yesterday.

94
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:08,580
You know how he is.

95
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:12,197
He'll disappear for a day or two
on a whim with no explanation.

96
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:13,520
Uh, he went south.

97
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:15,577
Isn't there a gate to
Cootie south of here?

98
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:16,490
You're right!

99
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:18,240
Damn it all!

100
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,197
I told him I would die for him!

101
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:22,927
And then I let him sneak
off to battle alone!

102
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:57,420
The place I entered was
like a different world.

103
00:06:57,920 --> 00:06:59,777
The stench of death filled the air,

104
00:06:59,860 --> 00:07:04,160
and a violent wave thick like
blood seemed to aim itself at me.

105
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:08,980
Time to say goodbye to
your head, Kozuki Oden.

106
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:43,460
Let's go!

107
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:52,100
I'm not alone!

108
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:55,277
There are people who live in this dream.

109
00:07:55,360 --> 00:08:01,917
I'm not sure if we were ever to come.

110
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,700
I'm not scared of me.

111
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:15,257
Thank

112
00:08:15,340 --> 00:08:16,657
you

113
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:23,740
so

114
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:35,739
much for watching.

115
00:08:57,340 --> 00:09:00,200
So you're the famous Kozuki Orenk!

116
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:03,500
I've been disavowed!

117
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:05,880
I no longer have a name.

118
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:10,440
Anyone can enter, but those who try
to leave will be promptly killed.

119
00:09:10,980 --> 00:09:13,740
Especially samurai like you.

120
00:09:19,740 --> 00:09:21,180
Sounds suffocating.

121
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:22,850
Huh?

122
00:09:22,933 --> 00:09:24,240
You've made a cage.

123
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:26,934
Watch in yourself when you can be free.

124
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:29,560
I didn't ask for your input. What?

125
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:34,317
You were foolish enough to come here,
so here you'll remain until your death.

126
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:36,282
Which I expect will be imminent.

127
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:39,300
So no one can leave.

128
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:41,000
Now it's personal!

129
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:43,300
That's my least favorite rule!

130
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:45,880
It's my turf, so they're my rules.

131
00:09:46,780 --> 00:09:47,780
Now die!

132
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:14,000
Whoa!

133
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:16,590
Whoa!

134
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:18,230
Whoa!

135
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:23,500
You run this hellhole! Hahaha! Ha,

136
00:10:25,580 --> 00:10:32,580
ha!

137
00:10:34,780 --> 00:10:35,610
Odin!

138
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:38,220
We're coming!

139
00:10:38,660 --> 00:10:40,072
Just stay where you are!

140
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:43,488
Look, he must have
broken through that gate!

141
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:55,497
This hellhole is the only
home that I will ever know.

142
00:10:55,580 --> 00:10:59,377
A pampered bastard like you
could never understand my life.

143
00:10:59,460 --> 00:11:02,920
Are you telling me this
is the life that you want?

144
00:11:04,780 --> 00:11:05,610
Look!

145
00:11:05,693 --> 00:11:06,540
He's up there!

146
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:08,680
Stop him!

147
00:11:19,820 --> 00:11:20,650
Odin!

148
00:11:20,860 --> 00:11:22,420
We'll help you fight!

149
00:11:25,980 --> 00:11:27,840
You're a moment too late.

150
00:11:28,180 --> 00:11:30,880
I just wrapped up here. My apologies.

151
00:11:31,780 --> 00:11:35,780
I fought all day and all
night, but it is done.

152
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:46,740
Why don't you kill me already?

153
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:49,840
I know there's no future for me.

154
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:52,680
I'll die with no regrets.

155
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:56,400
Is this Ashura Doji?

156
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:57,640
Their leader?

157
00:11:58,500 --> 00:12:00,360
Listen to me, all of you.

158
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:04,000
Are you still willing to
follow me to the bitter end?

159
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:10,920
I need your aid, your strength, your wit.

160
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:16,200
For I have decided to lift up
the people of this cursed land

161
00:12:17,300 --> 00:12:19,540
by becoming their king!

162
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:36,380
I come bearing news of young
Lord Odin What happened?

163
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:38,580
What did he do this time?

164
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:40,720
Take a look

165
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:47,640
Kuri has been tamed

166
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:54,900
Only Odin could accomplish this I
see it, but I can scarcely believe it

167
00:12:57,080 --> 00:13:01,760
The people of Kuri will ruff around the
edges but filled with boundless energy.

168
00:13:02,020 --> 00:13:05,017
Thanks to Odin's loyal companions
and headstrong leadership,

169
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:08,357
they turned their blood-soaked
land into a place worth living,

170
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:11,205
and the rest of Wano
could not help but notice.

171
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,600
In response to this accomplishment,

172
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:23,237
the shogun Kozuki Sukiyaki
retracted his disvowel.

173
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:26,720
and instead gave his son
the title Daimyo of Kuri.

174
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:28,070
Look!

175
00:13:28,153 --> 00:13:31,022
Lord Odin is going to be
a dying yo for real now!

176
00:13:31,700 --> 00:13:32,530
Yeah!

177
00:13:32,613 --> 00:13:34,377
Then Cootie will be a
full-fledged province!

178
00:13:34,460 --> 00:13:35,460
We pulled it off!

179
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:37,522
All that hard work was worth it!

180
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:43,520
King's all right.

181
00:13:47,260 --> 00:13:49,957
We knew you could do it
from the start, Lord Odin!

182
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:51,057
I'm so proud of you!

183
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:52,434
Congratulations, Odin!

184
00:13:52,620 --> 00:13:54,914
Now Cootie will finally be your winner!

185
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:01,080
All right, friends!

186
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:06,180
I'm the Gaimyo!

187
00:14:07,060 --> 00:14:07,890
Yeah!

188
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:21,000
You're looking dour, Asheran.

189
00:14:21,780 --> 00:14:23,320
This is new to me.

190
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:24,910
I...

191
00:14:24,993 --> 00:14:27,140
I have never known peace before.

192
00:14:29,860 --> 00:14:31,160
Thank you, Odin.

193
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:32,557
I owe you my...

194
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:33,660
Stop it!

195
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:34,980
You're creeping me!

196
00:14:38,820 --> 00:14:40,900
I was being sincere!

197
00:14:42,260 --> 00:14:43,090
Huh?

198
00:14:43,173 --> 00:14:44,580
What are you doing? No!

199
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:49,070
Stop!

200
00:14:49,153 --> 00:14:50,577
You should be celebrating!

201
00:14:50,660 --> 00:14:53,920
You know, a proper Daimyo needs retainers.

202
00:14:55,040 --> 00:14:58,140
I'm sure there are many
wise and prudent candidates.

203
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:02,700
But you're the only ones I want.

204
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:13,740
What say you?

205
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:15,400
Will you be my samurai?

206
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:40,940
No, it's not coming out of your noses!

207
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:42,000
No, it's on me!

208
00:15:42,640 --> 00:15:43,940
Disgusting! Stop!

209
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:48,520
Six years passed in Wano without incident.

210
00:15:49,500 --> 00:15:52,720
But across the seas, there
was a great storm brewing.

211
00:15:53,060 --> 00:15:55,100
33 years before the present day,

212
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:59,777
the remnants of the legendary rocks
pirates began to form into their own crews,

213
00:15:59,860 --> 00:16:01,957
with their strongest
members becoming infamous.

214
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:04,099
and influential in their own right.

215
00:16:11,020 --> 00:16:13,520
What are they? Animals?

216
00:16:14,580 --> 00:16:16,140
Just hairy men?

217
00:16:18,740 --> 00:16:21,000
What odd creatures they are.

218
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:28,980
Did you get it?

219
00:16:29,220 --> 00:16:30,100
Think so?

220
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:37,900
Long ago,

221
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:40,300
several hundred years ago in fact,

222
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:45,337
the Minx and the Kozuki samurai
from the land of Wano made a pledge.

223
00:16:45,420 --> 00:16:49,760
We swore to be steadfast
allies through thick and thin.

224
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:51,500
Stupid waddo!

225
00:16:51,660 --> 00:16:52,720
I hate it here!

226
00:16:52,960 --> 00:16:54,280
Dear country, stop!

227
00:16:54,460 --> 00:16:56,400
Get me down, dammit!

228
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:57,910
Help!

229
00:16:58,040 --> 00:16:59,500
I'm just a Cape!

230
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:00,816
You're all monsters!

231
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:03,637
We shouldn't have set
sail in the first place!

232
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:05,560
Coming here was a tough idea!

233
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:08,240
Some sworn allies you gotta are!

234
00:17:08,940 --> 00:17:11,820
A cat monster, a dog
monster, and a Cape too.

235
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:14,337
I'm starting to feel like
this whole beach is cursed.

236
00:17:14,420 --> 00:17:15,600
Let's burn them!

237
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:27,452
This should be enough fish for the vinyl!

238
00:17:31,980 --> 00:17:33,520
We're gonna die!

239
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:35,300
Help us!

240
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:36,780
Let them go!

241
00:17:46,860 --> 00:17:47,940
Such cruelty!

242
00:17:48,420 --> 00:17:49,360
Shame on you!

243
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:53,097
The only reason you fear them is
because they're different than you.

244
00:17:53,180 --> 00:17:56,617
But those are children you bastards
tried to burn at the stake!

245
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:57,920
Thank you, Kara!

246
00:18:00,300 --> 00:18:01,130
Farewell!

247
00:18:01,213 --> 00:18:03,022
You're just gonna leave us here!

248
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:12,920
Uh, why are there weird
little animals here?

249
00:18:13,100 --> 00:18:14,100
They followed me.

250
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:18,900
Thank you, Grove, for rescuing us!

251
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:21,930
Hot!

252
00:18:22,260 --> 00:18:24,677
Yeah, we almost starved,
we almost drowned,

253
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:27,348
and then we almost got
burned to death, too!

254
00:18:27,820 --> 00:18:28,650
Ah! Ah!

255
00:18:28,780 --> 00:18:29,610
Damn it!

256
00:18:29,693 --> 00:18:31,068
This is way too hot to eat!

257
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:33,400
Yeah, no, this is unnatural.

258
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:36,016
They should not be talking like that.

259
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:39,240
Ah, delightful.

260
00:18:39,800 --> 00:18:41,980
Father told me about minks like you.

261
00:18:42,140 --> 00:18:42,970
Then I was right!

262
00:18:43,053 --> 00:18:46,277
I knew as soon as I saw that
symbol, we had it back home, too.

263
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:48,597
where they say our
nations are like brothers.

264
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:50,033
Yugaru saved our lives.

265
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:52,520
We were so hungry. Of course.

266
00:18:52,860 --> 00:18:54,272
Eat as much as you like.

267
00:18:54,380 --> 00:18:55,620
Don't mind if I do.

268
00:18:57,140 --> 00:18:58,020
Like radish?

269
00:18:58,380 --> 00:18:59,740
You should try a bite.

270
00:18:59,940 --> 00:19:01,587
It does look good, actually.

271
00:19:02,260 --> 00:19:03,820
Now try the fish cake.

272
00:19:05,180 --> 00:19:06,160
How is it?

273
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:07,820
It's too hot!

274
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:15,680
Yes, it's not sensitive to us, okay?

275
00:19:16,320 --> 00:19:18,260
You've ruined it, you damn fool!

276
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:19,720
Oh, hey, stop it!

277
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:26,780
I'm sorry, Cat, but heat
is the spice of life!

278
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:29,680
And wooded was born to boil!

279
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:34,200
That's so cool!

280
00:19:35,220 --> 00:19:37,140
It tastes good to me.

281
00:19:37,760 --> 00:19:39,720
Who are you supposed to be?

282
00:19:39,880 --> 00:19:42,720
A castaway, in simple terms.

283
00:19:43,020 --> 00:19:45,240
My mother and I were shipwrecked.

284
00:19:45,360 --> 00:19:49,780
We asked for help, but people threw
rocks at us because we're fishmen.

285
00:19:50,740 --> 00:19:54,799
Unfortunately, my mother was struck
down, so we couldn't return home.

286
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:59,020
Before she died, she said to me,
The people above hate fishmen.

287
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:02,906
If you want to survive, then you
must tell them you're a kappa.

288
00:20:07,340 --> 00:20:08,980
I'm Kawamatsu the kappa.

289
00:20:09,280 --> 00:20:11,104
I've been living off leftovers.

290
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:14,157
Thank you for saving my life.

291
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:15,857
And thank you for treating me.

292
00:20:15,940 --> 00:20:17,137
To such a delicious meal.

293
00:20:17,220 --> 00:20:19,157
I will never forget this.

294
00:20:19,240 --> 00:20:22,037
May I eat the rest of the Odin now please?

295
00:20:22,120 --> 00:20:22,950
Not yet.

296
00:20:23,033 --> 00:20:25,077
We'll make some more, just wait.

297
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:26,797
That's not necessary.

298
00:20:26,880 --> 00:20:28,340
It's still edible.

299
00:20:29,900 --> 00:20:30,730
Oh no.

300
00:20:30,813 --> 00:20:32,977
I've been a bad guest haven't I?

301
00:20:33,060 --> 00:20:35,197
I wasted all that good food.

302
00:20:35,280 --> 00:20:37,120
You're being very mature.

303
00:20:39,740 --> 00:20:41,680
I am so sorry!

304
00:20:42,100 --> 00:20:43,120
I'll beat it!

305
00:20:45,560 --> 00:20:47,280
That's no way too hot!

306
00:20:49,440 --> 00:20:51,340
What a funny little creature!

307
00:20:52,740 --> 00:20:53,620
Stop it!

308
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:57,880
How splendid.

309
00:20:58,180 --> 00:21:01,062
The world is full of people
and creatures to see.

310
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:05,857
Meeting all of you has renewed my
determination to set sail and discover more!

311
00:21:05,940 --> 00:21:06,797
That's right!

312
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:08,757
This world's full of great stuff!

313
00:21:08,840 --> 00:21:10,380
Well, take care then.

314
00:21:11,380 --> 00:21:12,210
Huh?

315
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:14,090
Hey!

316
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:16,437
Didn't you go to hear us?

317
00:21:16,520 --> 00:21:18,520
We have nowhere else to go!

318
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:20,275
All right, all right!

319
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:21,820
Just get off of me!

320
00:21:25,580 --> 00:21:28,120
It happened again. Sure did!

321
00:21:28,380 --> 00:21:30,262
As you're terrible at saying no!

322
00:21:31,300 --> 00:21:34,537
Speaking of which, we really
need to talk about our finances.

323
00:21:34,620 --> 00:21:37,577
You've got to stop lending money
to Orochi without asking me.

324
00:21:37,660 --> 00:21:39,200
The guy's a total scumbag.

325
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:43,717
Well, even if he's independent now,
he's still one of Yasui's associates.

326
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:44,860
But he needs help.

327
00:21:50,360 --> 00:21:52,580
Sneaking, slinking, silence.

328
00:21:53,200 --> 00:21:54,030
Got it?

329
00:21:54,113 --> 00:21:56,380
Those are the basics. Yes, sir.

330
00:21:56,920 --> 00:21:59,540
Onward, think nothing of Yasui.

331
00:22:00,220 --> 00:22:02,800
Sneaking, slinking, silence.

332
00:22:10,860 --> 00:22:14,036
What were you thinking trying
to steal all this money?

333
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:16,517
Our Lord Odin's running
short on cash, okay?

334
00:22:16,600 --> 00:22:19,437
If you're gonna kill us, then
just do it, damn hedgehog.

335
00:22:19,520 --> 00:22:22,677
But you should know that we'd
do anything to help our Lord.

336
00:22:22,760 --> 00:22:25,540
I'll give my life if that's what it takes.

337
00:22:27,160 --> 00:22:28,320
What a mess.

338
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:31,040
Where do you find these people, Odin?

339
00:22:33,840 --> 00:22:36,080
I'll let you keep the stolen money.

340
00:22:38,620 --> 00:22:39,679
Please reconsider.

341
00:22:40,020 --> 00:22:42,608
Hakumai needs those
funds more than they do.

342
00:22:43,220 --> 00:22:44,050
Also...

343
00:22:46,380 --> 00:22:47,210
Here.

344
00:22:47,460 --> 00:22:50,440
While we're at it, take
this, too. It's yours.

345
00:22:50,720 --> 00:22:51,820
Wait, more money?

346
00:22:52,040 --> 00:22:53,857
There has to be some kind of catch.

347
00:22:53,940 --> 00:22:54,822
Is this a trap?

348
00:22:55,220 --> 00:22:57,520
Do you truly love Odin?

349
00:22:59,400 --> 00:23:03,700
If that's the case, then use this
money to clean yourselves up.

350
00:23:03,900 --> 00:23:08,580
Buy some books, learn some
manners, get educated.

351
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:11,360
Look at us!

352
00:23:19,200 --> 00:23:20,200
Yes, sir!

353
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:23,060
No, from the gut! Yes, sir!

354
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:36,080
Having a bunch of unruly thugs as
retainers will only bring shame to Odin.

355
00:23:36,340 --> 00:23:40,634
Lord Odin, I thank thee once more for
a bountiful feast on this fine day.

356
00:23:40,880 --> 00:23:43,060
Such piquancy, it's quite exquisite.

357
00:23:44,920 --> 00:23:46,280
What's gotten into you?

358
00:23:46,420 --> 00:23:48,126
Why are you talking that way?

359
00:23:48,220 --> 00:23:52,580
One day I'm sure he will become the
shogun of the land of Wano. Therefore,

360
00:23:52,880 --> 00:23:55,197
those who support him
must not only be loyal,

361
00:23:55,280 --> 00:23:58,240
They must be the finest
seminar in the country.

362
00:24:20,280 --> 00:24:23,717
It goes without saying that
you must protect your lord.

363
00:24:23,800 --> 00:24:27,280
But the people of Wano will
come to depend on you as well.

364
00:24:27,620 --> 00:24:31,540
You must be a symbol of our
strength, our guardian deity.

365
00:24:38,700 --> 00:24:42,112
The Daimyo of Kuri is making
a visit to the capital today.

366
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:46,200
I heard Lord Odin's retainers
are a bunch of thugs.

367
00:24:46,340 --> 00:24:47,340
Don't get robbed.

368
00:24:47,700 --> 00:24:50,465
Look, they're coming down
the street right now.

369
00:25:20,740 --> 00:25:23,700
Those are proper-looking samurais!

370
00:25:23,800 --> 00:25:26,740
Were Lord Odin's retainers
always so gallant?

371
00:25:26,980 --> 00:25:28,480
No, not like this.

372
00:25:28,660 --> 00:25:30,620
It's like a shogun's procession.

373
00:25:38,580 --> 00:25:42,357
The heroic side of these samurai
was such a wonder to behold

374
00:25:42,440 --> 00:25:46,820
that the entire capital seemed to
let on a collective gasp. Indeed,

375
00:25:47,080 --> 00:25:49,117
it was said that the
weight of their arrival was

376
00:25:49,200 --> 00:25:52,700
so great that the city
itself sunk ever so slightly.

377
00:25:56,360 --> 00:25:58,080
It's been a while, father.

378
00:25:58,540 --> 00:26:01,180
My son, what a welcome surprise.

379
00:26:01,500 --> 00:26:03,497
I hear you've become a great leader.

380
00:26:03,580 --> 00:26:05,377
My retainers have made me great.

381
00:26:05,460 --> 00:26:07,754
I'm no different than when I left here.

382
00:26:09,540 --> 00:26:11,620
You're showing gratitude to others?

383
00:26:12,060 --> 00:26:13,920
You don't need to be scared.

384
00:26:20,360 --> 00:26:24,237
Oden rushed to the capital when he
heard that his father had fallen ill.

385
00:26:24,320 --> 00:26:27,637
But seeing his son again seemed
to invigorate the Shogun.

386
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:32,440
However, this is the last time
that the two would exchange words.

387
00:26:35,560 --> 00:26:37,501
Seems people live on this island.

388
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:41,412
Pops, it's going to take at
least a week to patch this up.

389
00:26:41,720 --> 00:26:43,700
The water ruined all our cargo.

390
00:26:43,920 --> 00:26:46,740
First off, we need to
get food and supplies.

391
00:26:47,120 --> 00:26:48,120
Who wants to go?

392
00:26:48,740 --> 00:26:50,080
Most of us, probably.

393
00:26:50,560 --> 00:26:52,913
We all gotta stretch our legs, don't we?

394
00:26:57,140 --> 00:26:58,964
We just climbed up a waterfall.

395
00:27:03,280 --> 00:27:06,400
Yet there's sea here
and an island somehow.

396
00:27:12,780 --> 00:27:13,760
Trouble, sir.

397
00:27:14,020 --> 00:27:15,432
We need your help quick.

398
00:27:16,560 --> 00:27:17,620
What is it?

399
00:27:18,140 --> 00:27:19,000
Calm yourself.

400
00:27:19,160 --> 00:27:20,101
You're too loud.

401
00:27:20,420 --> 00:27:23,420
There's a giant pirate ship
ducked at Itachi board.

402
00:27:23,700 --> 00:27:25,220
A pirate ship?

403
00:27:30,340 --> 00:27:32,600
Lord Odin, where are you going?

404
00:27:33,060 --> 00:27:34,720
To the port!

405
00:27:36,660 --> 00:27:37,980
Go, go, go!

406
00:27:40,280 --> 00:27:41,340
All right, then.

407
00:27:41,560 --> 00:27:43,237
We'll go get food and supplies.

408
00:27:43,320 --> 00:27:45,620
And I'll come with you. No way.

409
00:27:45,860 --> 00:27:47,840
I told you no deckhands allowed.

410
00:27:48,120 --> 00:27:49,473
Ah, don't be like that.

411
00:27:49,580 --> 00:27:52,000
Hey, Pops, I can go with the crew, right?

412
00:27:52,300 --> 00:27:53,580
Do what you want.

413
00:27:55,080 --> 00:27:56,920
You heard us. Off we go!

414
00:27:57,640 --> 00:28:00,620
Yeah, and you heard me say no. Now stay.

415
00:28:01,280 --> 00:28:02,180
Wait, what?

416
00:28:02,520 --> 00:28:04,480
Port Odin ran off to the port.

417
00:28:05,620 --> 00:28:07,300
Why did you let him go?

418
00:28:07,780 --> 00:28:09,837
I heard a pirate ship
showed up out of nowhere.

419
00:28:09,920 --> 00:28:11,177
You say it looks real crazy!

420
00:28:11,260 --> 00:28:13,637
It's bigger than our ships,
and the pirates look tough.

421
00:28:13,720 --> 00:28:15,557
Stop him at any cost!

422
00:28:15,640 --> 00:28:18,037
Surely he's just going there
to take the pirates away?

423
00:28:18,120 --> 00:28:19,017
Not a chance!

424
00:28:19,100 --> 00:28:21,394
You know that this is his dream, right?

425
00:28:21,640 --> 00:28:23,400
He wants to set sail.

426
00:28:27,640 --> 00:28:29,057
That must be it.

427
00:28:29,140 --> 00:28:30,460
The pirate ship.

428
00:28:31,480 --> 00:28:32,310
Finally.

429
00:28:36,840 --> 00:28:38,457
Freedom—we're in trouble!

430
00:28:38,540 --> 00:28:39,370
All

431
00:28:40,720 --> 00:28:42,397
of you need to stand back;

432
00:28:42,480 --> 00:28:45,437
someone's coming for us,

433
00:28:45,520 --> 00:28:49,517
someone extraordinary—glad
you could make it!

434
00:28:49,600 --> 00:28:53,797
Breathing the storms, climbing the
waterfall—we don't get many visitors here.

435
00:28:53,880 --> 00:28:55,240
many visitors here

436
00:29:11,500 --> 00:29:13,177
Hello, pirates!

437
00:29:13,260 --> 00:29:15,380
I've been waiting for you!

438
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:35,980
I like you, old man!

439
00:29:36,600 --> 00:29:37,820
You're gonna pay!

440
00:29:40,600 --> 00:29:43,260
I'll teach you a thing or two, boy! Hey!

441
00:30:13,200 --> 00:30:15,965
I've been waiting for
someone like you, Pirate!

442
00:30:16,480 --> 00:30:18,600
My name is Press Gjolden!

443
00:30:18,800 --> 00:30:21,800
I don't know who you are,
but you're my ticket out!

444
00:30:22,020 --> 00:30:24,220
Take me with you! Huh?
